course: dictionary
lesson: 8782
title: Shale: a rock that splits into layers
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Shale is a rock. It is soft, grey or dark, and it is made of hardened mud or clay. «Shale and mudstone are made of very fine mud that settled in calm water, and they are the most common sedimentary rocks.» The clues are mud, settled and calm water, so shale began as mud at the bottom of quiet water.
explain: Shale splits easily into thin, flat layers, a bit like the pages of a book. When you see shale in a sentence, check whether the rest of the sentence talks about layers, mud or rocks. Those clues will tell you it is the rock, not a different word.
explain: Shale can also be a source of oil and gas, so companies drill into it to get them. In the news you may read «shale gas» or «fracking». Here shale means the rock where the gas is found. Phrases such as shale gas, shale oil and oil shale all show this meaning.
explain: Shale can change over time. «Slate is shale changed by pressure so that it splits into thin, flat sheets, which is why it is used for roofs.» The word slate is a clue: it comes from shale that has been changed by pressure, and it still splits into flat sheets.
fact: Shale is a soft grey or dark rock made of hardened mud or clay.
fact: Shale splits easily into thin, flat layers.
fact: Shale is a sedimentary rock, made when mud settles and is pressed over millions of years.
fact: Fossils are often found in shale, so it helps scientists learn about old living things.
fact: «Shale gas» is gas found in shale rock, and companies drill for it.
exercise: «Shale and mudstone are made of very fine mud that settled in calm water.» What is shale made of? | Melted glass | Sand from the beach | *Hardened mud or clay | Ice from a frozen lake
exercise: «Slate is shale changed by pressure so that it splits into thin, flat sheets, which is why it is used for roofs.» Why is slate used for roofs? | Because it grows on trees | Because it melts in the sun | Because it floats on water | *Because it splits into thin, flat sheets
exercise: A news reporter says «shale gas» is drilled for. What does shale mean here? | A soft drink | A kind of sea shell | A type of cloud | *A source of oil and gas that companies drill for
test: Why do scientists often find fossils in shale? | Because fossils melt shale into layers | Because shale is found only in deserts | Because shale is made of sugar | *Because shale formed from mud, which can trap the remains of old living things
test: What does «sedimentary» tell you about a rock like shale? | It was made from melted metal | It grew like a plant | It is a rock that has never been touched | *It was made when mud or sand settled and was pressed together
exam: «Metamorphic rocks are rocks changed by heat and pressure without melting, the way clay in a kiln turns into a hard pot: shale becomes slate.» What does shale become when heat and pressure change it? | Marble | *Slate | Chalk | Granite
